# Syntax: docs/LANGUAGE.md. Check with `rbb bid check`.
#
# Over their 1NT opening: what every defence shares (vs-1nt.notes.md).
#
# The card's `competitive.vs_1nt_strong.system` picks the
# defence, and each has its own module for the calls that differ:
# natural (overcalls.bid), Cappelletti and Modified Cappelletti
# (cappelletti.bid), DONT (dont.bid), Meckwell (meckwell.bid), Landy and
# Multi-Landy (multi-landy.bid). Their calls say what they show and set
# a question for partner (`sets ask=...`); the answers that are the same
# whichever defence asked are written here, once, against the question:
#
#   nt_majors       partner has both majors: pick one, invite or bid game
#   nt_mm(M)        partner has five M and a four-card minor
#   nt_which_minor  I asked for that minor: partner names it
#   nt_minors       partner has both minors: pick one
#   nt_pc(x)        partner has x and another suit: pass, or ask which
#   nt_other        I asked for the other suit: partner names it
#   nt_one(x)       partner has shown one long suit x
#   nt_penalty      partner doubled for penalties
#
# Advancer's strength is measured in support points (tp) once a major
# fits. BBA (21GF-DEFAULT, probes/vs-1N-capp-*-adv.toml) raises a
# five-card major with 3+ support: to three with 8-14 total points and
# to game from about 11. The overcaller has 9-17, so we invite with 10-12
# support points and bid game from 13.

module vs-1nt "Over their 1NT: what every defence shares"
  needs  base
  skill  competitive_bidding/defense_vs_1nt
  param  def       = competitive.vs_1nt_strong.system default other
  param  dont_play = competitive.dont.play default false

# ── Preempts and the pass ────────────────────────────────────────────
# With a conventional defence a seven-card suit jumps to the three level
# only when it is too weak for the one-suited call: BBA on 21GF-DEFAULT
# preempts with 6-8 HCP and bids 2♣ (Cappelletti) from 9 with seven cards
# (probes/vs-1N-capp.toml). We preempt up to 11 counting a point a card
# beyond four, one below the one-suiter's 12: 4-8 HCP with seven cards.
# The natural defence keeps its own 4-10 (overcalls.bid).
after (1N) when !(def is other) | dont_play
  3S  "Preemptive: seven spades"                  shows S>=7, hcp>=4, hcp+length_points<=11
      priority 1
  3H  "Preemptive: seven hearts"                  shows H>=7, hcp>=4, hcp+length_points<=11
      priority 1
  3D  "Preemptive: seven diamonds"                shows D>=7, hcp>=4, hcp+length_points<=11
      priority 1
  3C  "Preemptive: seven clubs"                   shows C>=7, hcp>=4, hcp+length_points<=11
      priority 1
after (1N) | (1N) P (P)
  P   "Nothing to say over their 1NT"             priority -10

# ── Partner has both majors ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Cappelletti 2♦, Landy and Multi-Landy 2♣, DONT 2♥, Meckwell X then 2♥.
# Preference to the longer major (hearts when equal, as BBA and GIB),
# a jump to invite with four, game from 13 support points; a long minor
# with at most two cards in either major plays there.
when asked nt_majors, rho.last=P | rho.last=X
  P   "Hearts: to play"                  shows H>=S
      when  partner.last=2H
  2H  "Preference: hearts"               shows H>=S
  2S  "Preference: spades"               shows S>H
  3H  "Invitational: four hearts"        shows H>=4, H>=S, tp(H)=10..12
  3S  "Invitational: four spades"        shows S>=4, S>H, tp(S)=10..12
  4H  "Game in hearts"                   shows H>=3, H>=S, tp(H)>=13
  4S  "Game in spades"                   shows S>=3, S>H, tp(S)>=13
  P   "Long clubs: to play"              shows C>=6, H<=2, S<=2
      when  partner.last=2C
  P   "Long diamonds: to play"           shows D>=6, H<=2, S<=2
      when  partner.last=2D
  3C  "Long clubs: to play"              shows C>=6, H<=2, S<=2
      when  !partner.last=2C
  3D  "Long diamonds: to play"           shows D>=6, H<=2, S<=2
      when  !partner.last=2D

# ── Partner has five of a major and a four-card minor ────────────────
# Cappelletti and Multi-Landy 2♥/2♠, Modified Cappelletti 2♣ then 2♥/2♠.
# Pass with two or more; raise with three; 2NT asks for the minor with a
# singleton or void; a six-card suit of my own is to play.
when asked nt_mm(M), rho.last=P | rho.last=X
  P    "{M} to play"                            shows M>=2
  3{M} "Invitational raise"                     shows M>=3, tp(M)=10..12
  4{M} "Game in {M}"                            shows M>=3, tp(M)>=13
  2N   "Which is your minor?"                   alert  artificial
       shows M<=1
       sets  ask=nt_which_minor
  2S   "Six or more spades: to play"            shows S>=6, M<=2
       when  M is H
  3H   "Six or more hearts: to play"            shows H>=6, M<=2
       when  M is S
  3C   "Six or more clubs: to play"             shows C>=6, M<=1
  3D   "Six or more diamonds: to play"          shows D>=6, M<=1

when asked nt_which_minor, rho.last=P | rho.last=X
  3C  "My minor is clubs"                       shows C>=4, C>=D
  3D  "My minor is diamonds"                    shows D>=4, D>C

# ── Partner has both minors ──────────────────────────────────────────
# 2NT in Cappelletti, Meckwell and Multi-Landy. The longer minor, and
# diamonds when equal (BBA, probes/vs-1N-capp-2N-adv.toml: 98 of 98);
# game with a fit and 14 support points.
when asked nt_minors, rho.last=P | rho.last=X
  3C  "Preference: clubs"                       shows C>D
  3D  "Preference: diamonds"                    shows D>=C
  5C  "Game in clubs"                           shows C>=4, C>D, tp(C)>=14
  5D  "Game in diamonds"                        shows D>=4, D>=C, tp(D)>=14
  3H  "Six or more hearts: to play"             shows H>=6, C<=2, D<=2
  3S  "Six or more spades: to play"             shows S>=6, C<=2, D<=2

# ── Partner has a known suit and another ─────────────────────────────
# DONT 2♣/2♦ (and a higher suit), Meckwell 2♣/2♦ (and a major). Pass
# with three of the known suit; otherwise the next step asks for the
# other one, which partner passes or corrects.
when asked nt_pc(x), rho.last=P | rho.last=X
  P   "Support for {x}: to play"                shows x>=3
  2D  "Which is your other suit?"               alert
      shows x<=2
      when  x is C
      sets  ask=nt_other
  2H  "Which is your other suit? (pass or correct)"   alert
      shows x<=2
      when  x is D
      sets  ask=nt_other

when asked nt_other, rho.last=P | rho.last=X
  P   "My other suit is diamonds"               shows D>=4
      when  partner.last=2D
  P   "My other suit is hearts"                 shows H>=4
      when  partner.last=2H
  2H  "My other suit is hearts"                 shows H>=4
  2S  "My other suit is spades"                 shows S>=4

# ── Partner has shown one long suit ──────────────────────────────────
# After a relay answer, a natural 2♥/2♠ (Meckwell, DONT 2♠) or the
# Multi-Landy 2♦. Raise a major with two or more: invite with 11-12,
# game from 13.
when asked nt_one(x), rho.last=P | rho.last=X
  3{x} "Invitational raise"                     shows x>=2, hcp=11..12
       when  x is H | x is S
  4{x} "Game in {x}"                            shows x>=2, hcp>=13
       when  x is H | x is S
  P    "Nothing more to say"                    priority -5

# ── Partner doubled for penalties ────────────────────────────────────
# Cappelletti and Modified Cappelletti: 15+ HCP. Sit with five or more
# HCP, or with nowhere to go; run to a five-card suit with less.
when asked nt_penalty, rho.last=P | rho.last=XX
  P   "Sitting for the penalty double"          priority -1
  2C  "Weak: five or more clubs"                shows C>=5, hcp<=4
  2D  "Weak: five or more diamonds"             shows D>=5, hcp<=4
  2H  "Weak: five or more hearts"               shows H>=5, hcp<=4
  2S  "Weak: five or more spades"               shows S>=5, hcp<=4
